  "rationale": "Two independent leased source reviews support the registered program-specific metric-to-species interpretation for historical positive composite-apiary occurrences. The later genus wording is retained explicitly, not presented as literal binomial data. Positive parasite detections in managed hosts qualify as sampled occurrence, without a claim of wild establishment, local acquisition, or continued presence. Full immutable snapshot scanning preserves all selected county rows. County identities must resolve uniquely in current geography; former Connecticut counties and ambiguous county/city names remain excluded. Kauai and Maui positives are held for the specific contradictory survey context. No other measurement column or zero result is admitted by this positive method.",
